Selected FEX upstream DiskCache backports for FEX-2609.1 (9fbdc00bd6401aff3b32d79e78ff98b8a13e4dcf).
Apply after the six existing Darwin patches; independent of PCMP instruction changes.
Upstream provenance (FEX-Emu/FEX), dependency order:
  7a82b07bfd59670116e0b99006c89aa140e98e01 DiskCache: optional memory buffer for faster lookups
  83d8317dae95fd2c1c70a5be1a04dfec5a68d865 DiskCache: configurable max file size
  b37aae728f496c6419a1defa0bcbdc74eaea531b DiskCache: adjust key strategy
  ae3a4ae1974186afea73af67417e3ec634412a1e FEXCore: Adds a utility function for deleting a directory
  47bc73575e8d61d04950c4347570af2d970bd09a FEXCore/FileUtils: Adds a way to walk a directory with callback
  47557a6184f501fd283e2e5c10298f3010fca47d FEXCore/DiskCache: Prune old entries automatically
  f3b0b412548e45843470ef2b3bef1af0f26ea0f3 Win32: Implement RemoveDirectory
  7962f4006565272b7b0c8c1ae1536a2a3d1a0e22 FileUtils: Implement RecursiveRemoveDirectory and WalkDirectory with NT syscalls

Release adaptations: retain public DiskCache header, GuestBase translations, and existing codegen.
Correct strict FOZ cap accounting under lock (including wrappers and mapping-off writes); atomic full flag.
Snapshot lookup candidates under IndexLock; match memory entries by footprint as well as guest hash.
Create an eviction worker for read-only LRU use; include list explicitly.
Fix NT directory buffer growth shadowing and open directories without following reparse points.
Translate the WoW64 guest span before cache hashing/copying in Core.cpp.
Keep the serialized header when promoting a disk hit into the memory LRU.
DiskCache remains opt-in; memory LRU defaults to zero bytes; main-file cap defaults to 1 GiB.
Owned FormatVersion 0xA609 uses the existing uint16_t field with its high bit set.
It invalidates baseline and upstream caches for combined Darwin, ThreadTerm, and PCMP IR/constants changes.
This patch does not assert compatibility with caches generated by upstream main.

